From: kevinzhow <kevinzhow@local>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:21:26 +0900
Subject: Mobile file dialog: suggest the name the application asks for

SaveFile's mobile path left current_name out ("not implemented"): the file name field stayed
empty, so a Qt application's proposed name (untitled.kra, say) never showed and the user or the
agent had to type one. Without current_file, the dialog now gets current_name as its current file,
in current_folder or else the home folder it opens in; setCurrentFile already puts the name into
the field and switches into that folder. Only the name part is used (the portal specifies a name).

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-01
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [a plain gap; check upstream master first]
X-Rungic-Tests: none (gap: checked by hand on the phone, docs/103)
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/103
---
 src/filechooser.cpp | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/filechooser.cpp b/src/filechooser.cpp
index 025dfc7..e94fa19 100644
--- a/src/filechooser.cpp
+++ b/src/filechooser.cpp
@@ -574,10 +574,13 @@ void FileChooserPortal::SaveFile(const QDBusObjectPath &handle,
 
         if (!currentFile.isEmpty()) {
             m_mobileFileDialog->setCurrentFile(currentFile);
+        } else if (!currentName.isEmpty()) {
+            // The suggested name in the file name field, in the suggested folder or else the home
+            // folder the dialog opens in: setCurrentFile takes a path and does both.
+            const QString folder = currentFolder.isEmpty() ? QStandardPaths::writableLocation(QStandardPaths::HomeLocation) : currentFolder;
+            m_mobileFileDialog->setCurrentFile(QDir(folder).filePath(QFileInfo(currentName).fileName()));
         }
 
-        // currentName: not implemented
-
         if (!acceptLabel.isEmpty()) {
             m_mobileFileDialog->setAcceptLabel(acceptLabel);
         }
